<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 95 0 R
/T (In these experiments, the process system calls getpid\(\), getppid\(\), fork\(\), wait\(\) and exec\(\), and the file system calls open\(\), write\(\), read\(\) and close\(\), were run through Python's os module on Linux. The experiments show how a process is created, how a parent synchronizes with its child, how a process image is replaced, and how files are handled at the system call level. )
/E (In these experiments, the process system calls getpid\(\), getppid\(\), fork\(\), wait\(\) and exec\(\), and the file system calls open\(\), write\(\), read\(\) and close\(\), were run through Python's os module on Linux. The experiments show how a process is created, how a parent synchronizes with its child, how a process image is replaced, and how files are handled at the system call level. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [30]
>>
